hlight\uc2 \f2  weak.\par     Story: Related stories: \par     \par     O2 CR: Shares in \f28 \uc2 \f2 O2 Czech Republic\f28 \uc2 \f2  SPTT.PR climbed 3 percent\par on Tuesday after the telecoms operator said it would propose\par paying part of its share premium on top of a 2016 dividend.   \par     Story: Related stories: \par     \par     CEE MARKETS: The forint retreated and Hungarian government\par yields steadied at record lows on Tuesday as the country's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut its short-term lending rates, whileassets in\par Central Europe's fast-growing emerging economies were mixed.\par     Story: Related stories: \par ---------------------- MARKET SNAPSHOT ------------------------\par  Index/Crown \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest     Prev   Pct change Pct change\par                                     close    on day     in 2016\par  vs Euro        27.019     27.012    -0.03     -0.08\par  vs Dollar         24.777     24.859     0.33      0.34\par  Czech Equities    934.05     934.05     -0.14     -2.33\par  U.S. Equities 18,169.27  18,223.03     -0.3       4.27\par  Pvs close or current levels vs prior domestic close at 1500 GMT\par ======================PRESS DIGEST=============================\par     VITKOVICE: State-owned Czech Export Bank and EGAP insurer\par claim 15.5 billion crowns ($625.58 million) from Vitkovice Power\par Engineering, currently in insolvency, for the financing the CEB\par provided for a power plant project in Turkey.\par     Mlada Fronta Dnes, page 9\par        \par    (Reuters has not verified the stories, nor does it vouch for\par their accuracy.)\par                    \par  For real-time stock market index quotes click in brackets: \par  Warsaw WIG20  Budapest BUX Prague PX \par  For updates on CEE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                        \par  TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets         