\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Czech c.banker says need to see inflation above target to exit  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  policy\b0\par\par\uc2 463 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2015\par 23:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, estimated volume of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 PRAGUE, Sept 15 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Czech Republic\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to see inflation overshooting its 2 percent target in its policy forecasts before it considers exiting its weak crown policy, board member Jiri Rusnok was quoted as saying on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has pledged to keep the crown on the weak side of around 27 to the euro until at least the second half of 2016 to spur price growth.\par \par \uc2 Rusnok said the timing of the exit depended on future forecasts and reiterated the bank never ruled out delaying it.\par \par \uc2 "The forecasts quite evolve, although the moves are small, by tenths (of percentage points)," he said in an interview with Hospodarske Noviny due to be published on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "We have to take it seriously. We never ruled out we could exit the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  later. We have always said 'minimum' or 'at least'."\par \par \uc2 The bank has forecast inflation, which slowed to an annual rate of 0.3 percent in August, reaching its target only in early 2017. Asked about the chances of an exit in 2017, Rusnok said it would rely on future forecasts.\par \par \uc2 "It will be key for us to see a clear reaching, but I would say overshooting, of the inflation target in the horizon of 12 to 18 months," Rusnok said.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation should head above 2 percent, that means between 2 and 3 percent."\par \par \uc2 After launching the policy in 2013, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has only now had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the crown at bay after it firmed this year thanks to an accelerating economy whose pace is among the fastest in the \uc2 European Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bank first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in mid-July. Data released last week showed it bought 1 billion euros that month.\par \par \uc2 Analysts estimate it tripled that amount in August and has accelerated the tactic even more this month. ING estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  printed 60 billion crowns (2.22 billion euros) in early September.\par \par \uc2 Rusnok echoed remarks by Governor Miroslav Singer - who will be replaced by Rusnok next July - that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not have to worry about its reserves.\par \par \uc2 "Should we get somewhere around the half of GDP, that would still be reserves of an acceptable level for a country of our type," he said.\par \par \uc2 "I don't see anything wrong with having very decent \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves."\par \par \uc2 Rusnok said that the pressure for more monetary easing was less than half a year ago but said he could not rule out the option of negative interest rates if they were needed. (Reporting by Robert Muller and Jason Hovet; Editing by Hugh Lawson and Jonathan Oatis) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-9-15T22:08:23.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150915eb9f00pme\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
