\par\par \b \uc2 CEE Morning Briefing: \uc2 Hungary  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  in Focus\b0\par\par\uc2 By Margit Feher and Leos Rousek   \par \uc2 443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 2015\par 06:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \par Local/GMT \par 1400/1200 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungary \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central \par           bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate call \par 1500/1300 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungary \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central \par           bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  statement \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hungary is widely expected to continue its easing cycle on Tuesday as its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has weathered the financial market storm caused by the Greek crisis relatively well.\f28 \par \par \uc2 "Things have turned slightly worse but remain at very supportive levels. Put simply, we think the \uc2 Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cares that Hungary is not standing out in risk-terms versus peers, especially as it moves to cut [interest rates] below [those of regional peer] Poland," said Nonumar economist Peter Attard Montalto.\par \par \uc2 Poland's benchmark monetary policy rate is at 1.5%, the same as Hungary's key rate. But both are still above the Czech Republic's headline rate of 0.05% and near-zero interest rates in the euro area, the main trading partner for all economies in Central Europe.\par \par \uc2 Hungary is set to cut its main rate to a fresh record low, albeit at a slower pace than in each of the previous three months, 15 of the 17 economists polled said. Most of them forecast a 0.10 percentage-point easing this time around, compared with the 0.15-percentage-point moves in each of the previous three months.\par \par \uc2 The Hungarian easing cycle is predicted to bottom out at either 1.2% or 1.3%. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par EUR/CZK \par 0350 GMT 27.060-122 \par Previous 27.056-118 \par %Chg +0.01 \par  \par EUR/HUF \par 0350 GMT  309.69-10.21 \par Previous  309.81-10.33 \par %Chg -0.04 \par  \par  \par EUR/PLN \par 0350 GMT  4.1235-51 \par Previous  4.1236-52 \par %Chg 0.00 \par  \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par Hungary \par           Mon    Fri \par 3 yrs    2.05%  2.03% \par 5 yrs    2.75%  2.75% \par 10yrs    3.63%  3.66% \par  \par Poland \par           Mon    Fri \par 3 yrs    1.78%  1.77% \par 5 yrs    2.31%  2.32% \par 10yrs    2.87%  2.89% \par  \par Czech Republic \par           Mon    Fri \par 3 yrs    0.17%  0.13% \par 5 yrs    0.40%  0.41% \par 10yrs    1.17%  1.13% \par  \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG 20 \par 2,244.63  -40.40  -1.77% \par  \par BUX \par 22,475.89  -14.33  -0.06% \par  \par PX \par 1,030.18  +5.24  +0.51% \par  \par  \par OTHER NEWS \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CZECH REPUBLIC\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  last week \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets--the first time since imposing a ceiling for the koruna against the euro in November 2013, the bank's spokeswoman said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Margit Feher at margit.feher@wsj.com and Leos Rousek at leos.rousek@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 July 21, 2015 00:22 ET (04:22 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150721eb7l000b8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
