\par\par \uc2 Top Stories\par \b \uc2 Czech  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Willing to Resume  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 BY SEAN CARNEY   \par \uc2 607 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2015\par 18:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Top Global Market Stories\par \uc2 DJTGMS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 PRAGUE--The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest measures to combat eurozone deflation are taking their toll on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Czech Republic\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whose \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday warned that it may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to keep the koruna weak against the euro.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also extended the duration of keeping the koruna weak from the previously stated exit date of early 2016 until at least the second half of next year, and possibly for the duration of the year.\par \par \uc2 The weakening euro and falling oil prices are creating "unusually high levels of uncertainty" and adding fresh downward pressure to Czech prices, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Miroslav Singer said, adding that as a result the bank expects deflation later this year.\par \par \uc2 That is a cold shower for the bank which was forced to devalue the koruna in late 2013 after earlier setting its interest rates at near zero levels.\par \par \uc2 In November 2013, the \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent more than EUR7 billion in a one-day assault on markets that weakened the koruna more than 5% against the euro, staved off domestic deflation, and pulled the country out of a two-year long recession. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said at the time it wouldn't allow the koruna to firm beyond 27 against the euro.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark interest rate is 0.05%, making it the loosest monetary policy east of the eurozone. The monetary policy board says it won't move into negative interest rates.\par \par \uc2 So with deflation looming, the only primary tool left to further ease monetary conditions is another devaluation. Mr. Singer is ready to act if needed.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to move the exchange rate commitment to a weaker level if there were to be a long-term increase in deflationary pressures capable of causing a slump in domestic demand, renewed risks of deflation in the Czech economy and a systematic decrease in inflation expectations," Mr. Singer said.\par \par \uc2 Unlike in most countries in central Europe, Czech inflation was accelerating for most of 2014. But as of late, consumer price growth has stagnated and deflationary tendencies are looming largely due to the euro's weakness. Since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2013 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro has lost over 15% to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday afternoon the koruna was trading steadily at 27.72 to the euro. Some analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is too strong at current levels and barring another devaluation, prices are bound to decline.\par \par \uc2 William Jackson\uc2 , analyst at Capital Economics in London, said it is looking increasingly likely that Czechs will weaken the koruna, and he suggested 29 to the euro as an estimate.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Singer said it is impossible to predict where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will set a new ceiling, saying the scope of such a policy step would be determined later by market sentiment, market interest rates and other macroeconomic factors.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has an inflation target of 2% and on Thursday said it now expects consumer price growth of 1.1% in the first quarter of next year and 1.6% in the second quarter. The bank previously forecast inflation at 2.1% and 2.3%, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Negative spillover from the ECB's quantitative easing policy is also being felt in Denmark, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday cut its deposit rate for the fourth time in less than three weeks. It has also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  multiple times on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent the krone from appreciating to what would be painful levels for the economy.\par \par \uc2 Write to Sean Carney at sean.carney@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJTGMS1120150205eb25000cw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
