\par\par \b \uc2 Poland, Hungary Should Follow Czech in Curbing Deflation -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,593 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2015\par 09:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0805 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The \uc2 Czech National Bank\uc2 's policy mix of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and near-zero interest rates--in place since late 2013 and late 2012, respectively--may serve a model for Poland and Hungary in their battles against deflation, says \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  analyst \uc2 Pasquale Diana\uc2 . "Central banks that are really keen to bring inflation back to target ought to target weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 , either via cutting rates aggressively, or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or both," Diana says. "The CNB in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Czech Republic\b0 \highlight\uc2  shows an interesting example of how successful this policy can be in a small, open economy." In comparison with its regional peers Czech "core goods inflation has turned positive and even accelerated recently," he says, adding that it became evident after the CNB sold koruna worth about EUR7 billion on open markets to devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by about 5% to stoke inflationary pressures through higher prices of imports. (leos.rousek@wsj.com, @LeoRousek) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0759 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Philippines shares continued their ascent to record levels Tuesday, with the PSEi closing 0.6% higher to a new all-time high 7630.57. "Investor interest continues to be fuelled by expectations of good 2014 economic data and revenue growth. We are also pleased to note that fund managers remain upbeat about the market's prospects," said PSE chief executive \uc2 Hans Sicat\uc2  in a statement. GDP data are due Thursday and economists in a Wall Street Journal poll project a 5.8% growth for 4Q, faster than 3Q's 5.3%. Volume is moderately heavy, with gainers narrowly edging out losers, 96 to 93. Advancers are led by \uc2 Security Bank\uc2  (SECB.PH), up 1.4% to PHP149.50 after the lender announced a plan to issue USD-denominated benchmark bond; \uc2 Metropolitan Bank & Trust\uc2  (MBT.PH), up 3.1% to PHP98; and Bloomberry Resorts (BLOOM.PH), up 0.5% to PHP12.94 after reporting a purchase of a 12-hectare land in South Korea for a leisure and tourism project. Traders expect the next resistance for the PSEi at 7800, then at 8000; immediate support is placed at 7500.(cris.larano@dowjones.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0753 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--EUR/USD settled in to a tight range overnight showing little damage from the Greek political situation. USD/RUB jumped close to 9%, hitting a fresh 1-month high of 69.31 after \f28 \uc2 \f2 S&P\f28 \uc2 \f2  cut Russia to junk at BB+ late Monday. USD/JPY ran into profit taking at 118.50 and fell further after Japan's economy minister said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was not constrained by a loose schedule of about two years for achieving its 2% inflation goal. EUR/CHF perked up after the SNB's Danthine warned it's ready to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The main bourses ended Monday with small gains, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 S&P\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nasdaq\f28 \uc2 \f2  +0.3%, the Nikkei closed 1.7% higher. Up ahead, the first look at UK 4Q GDP (0930 GMT) and U.S. durable goods (1330GMT) are the data highlights. U.S. markets are likely to thinned by bad weather. gary.stride@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0751 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--UK growth is expected to have slowed in the 4Q with existing data showing both industrial production and construction output fell in November, while service sector data is the unknown and will be published alongside the GDP report at 0930 GMT. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  survey forecast for 4Q GDP is for rises of 0.6% q-q and 2.8% y-y, from +0.7% and +2.6% respectively for 3Q. gary.stride@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0750 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Turkey's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will signal looser monetary policies and lower its 6.1% yearend inflation forecast for 2015, as oil is trading at almost half the $92-per-barrel price policy-makers used in their October inflation report, say Tera Brokers analysts in Istanbul. "Markets will be watching Governor [Erdem] Basci's comments regarding the path of interest rates going forward," as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unveils its inflation report at 0800 GMT, the analysts say. "Basci will sound dovish in tandem with globally low rates environment benign prospects for headline and core CPI at home," Tera adds, forecasting a continuing rally in bonds and equities. Benchmark two-year bonds ended Monday at 6.73%, their first close below 7% since June 19, 2013. (emre.peker@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0741 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Thanks to the ECB's latest stimulus announcement, investors appear pretty comfortable with emerging markets in Asia these days. Stock benchmarks in the Philippines, India and Indonesia are all trading near record highs. And Asia's second-best performing index year-to-date is the frontier market of Pakistan. The benchmark Pakistan KSE 100 is already up more than 7%. The only market to top that is Shenzhen, where speculation by local Chinese moms and pops continues to pump up mainland shares. The Shenzhen's index is up nearly 10%. (chao.deng@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0738 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China government bonds are down as the market has priced in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's move to offer longer-term liquidity via 28-day reverse repos. The seven-year government bond yield is up at 3.39% vs 3.36% late Monday. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  offered CNY30 billion of seven-day reverse repos and CNY30 billion of 28-day reverse repos in Tuesday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , its first use of the 28-day tool since Jan. 8, 2013. "It offered the investors an excuse to push the bonds up yesterday, but it's actually not that encouraging since it's just money injection to meet demand ahead of the Lunar New Year holiday," says a Shanghai-based local bank trader. (wynne.wang@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: TAG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0733 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Like Greece, Spain could see a left-wing government come into power this year with the current encumbents unlikely to secure a second term of office, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Says that, while a left-wing government is unlikely to choke off any economic upturn, political uncertainties do provide an argument that Spanish bonds should tend to underperform their counterparts from other periphery countries ahead of the elections. 10-year Spain yields 1.38% and 10-year Greece yields 8.92%. (nick.cawley@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0725 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Barack Obama says the breakthrough between the U.S. and India in implementing the civil nuclear agreement between the two nations will mean "more reliable electricity for Indians and cleaner non-carbon energy" that helps fight climate change. "Students will be able to study at nights," he says. "Businesses [will] be able to stay open longer and hire more workers. Farmers [will] be able to use mechanized tools that increases their productivity." Obama says the U.S. is also keen to partner with India in plans to grow electricity generation from renewable sources, such as wind and solar. (saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; @journosaurabh) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0720 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Thailand's exports are still expected to make a mild recovery in 2015 despite a slight contraction in 2014. The commerce ministry's latest report shows the country's overseas shipments registered a 1.9% increase in December from a year earlier, while trade account balance reverted to a surplus of $1.58 billion. But for the whole of 2014, Thai exports contracted 0.41% and trade balance recorded a deficit of 378 million in 2014. "After a two-year streak of flat growth, we expect Thai exports to post mild growth of 4% this year, supported by a more visible and strong recovery in the U.S. economy and continued rising demand from CLMV (Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar and Vietnam) countries," says TISCO Economic Strategy Unit in Bangkok. (nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: ALP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0702 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Copper prices remained marginally down in late Asia trade, after slipping earlier in the day. Dollar strength and plunging crude oil prices have clouded the outlook for copper, but speculation that China's State Reserve bureau will stock up to take advantage of low prices has lent some support to the metal. At 0640 GMT, three-month copper prices on the London Metal Exchange were at $5,570/ton, down 0.6% from the opening price.(biman.mukherji@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0659 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] A bearish Tuesday close for USD/KRW suggests that the South Korea won may gain to 1,070 versus the U.S. dollar in the near term. The greenback began the day on a firm footing but later retreated as lead indicator USD/JPY subsided. Tuesday's closing of 1,079.8 places USD/KRW underneath the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone --a bearish technical signal. But the pair now rests at the entrance to the daily Bollinger downtrend channel at 1,079.8. If this technical support is also broken Wednesday, the downtrend channel will come back into effect and lead the way to the round-figure trading barrier at 1,070. USD/KRW closed at 1,079.8 versus its Monday close of 1,080.8. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 27, 2015 03:05 ET (08:05 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150127eb1r000uy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
