\par\par \b \uc2 Czech Koruna Again A Regional Safe Haven -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 202 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 2015\par 13:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1211 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--The Czech koruna is regaining its title as central European \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  safe haven following sharp drops on neighboring \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after today's Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement, says Jan Vejmelek, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Komercni Banka\uc2 . The koruna is bolstered thanks to previous \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves that helped the \b \highlight22\uc2 Czech Republic\b0 \highlight\uc2  avoid deflation. In Nov. '13 the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, weakening the koruna over 5% to the euro, which boosted inflation and prevented a deflationary spiral. The \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  established a koruna trading range and that should hold in coming days, Mr. Vejmelek says. Risks mainly come ahead of the EBC's meeting next week where it might launch QE, and ahead of the \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Feb. 5 meeting where it'll should announce a weaker inflation outlook but likely keep monetary policy unchanged, he says. EUR/CZK trades 0.5% firmer on the day against the euro at 27.91. (sean.carney@dowjones.com; @SeanCarneyWSJ) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 15, 2015 07:11 ET (12:11 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150115eb1f001fw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\