\par\par \b \uc2 Czech c.bank governor says sees smooth exit from  \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 176 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2014\par 15:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 HRADEC KRALOVE, \b \highlight22\uc2 Czech Republic\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Sept 9 (Reuters) - Exit from the \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's mode of keeping the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exchange rate weak will be smooth and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can act easily on the market to help avoid any big fluctuations, Governor \uc2 Miroslav Singer\uc2  said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The bank has kept a lid on the exchange rate since \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the crown last November, pledging to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firms below around 27 to the euro as part of its monetary policy easing, and plans to maintain that policy until 2016.\par \par \uc2 "I believe the exit will be relatively smooth, if not, then it is easy to solve, as everybody already knows," Singer said.\par \par \uc2 Exit should not bring any big jumps in part because traders do not have enough room to build big speculative positions due to tougher regulation, he said at a debate with businessmen. (Reporting by Robert Muller, writing by Jan Lopatka) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-9-9T14:48:25.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140909ea9900dxz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
