\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 2-Leu down a touch after rate cut, c.banks in focus\b0\par\par\uc2 738 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2013\par 15:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Romanian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cuts rates, space for more narrows\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Polish, Czech central banks meeting this week\par     * Telefonica CR shares fall after PPF deal\par     By Marton Dunai and Jason Hovet\par     BUDAPEST/PRAGUE, Nov 5 (Reuters) - The leu fell a touch on\par Tuesday when the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut interest rates to a\par new record low, the first in a series rate setting meetings in\par central Europe this week.\par     With rates across the region falling to record lows in the\par past year, borrowing costs have likely reached or are near\par bottom as economies look to re-gain some traction after slowing\par in the wake of the euro zone crisis.\par     The space for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Romania's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cut interest rates\par has narrowed but the bank could still use other tools to ease\par monetary policy, Governor Mugur Isarescu said on Tuesday.\par     Markets will also look to a rate decision on Wednesday in\par Poland, where rates are unlikely to go any lower, and on\par Thursday in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Czech Republic\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , where the threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as a tool to ease policy is weighing on the crown.\par     In the Czech Republic, data on Tuesday showed retail sales\par rose by an annual 3.7 percent in September, in line with\par forecasts. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts said a recovery in consumption reduced\par the chance of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (CNB) to weaken\par the crown. "The CNB is unlikely to initiate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," BNP\par said. "This is the main premise for trading the CZK markets."\par     By 1413 GMT, the crown had dipped less than 0.1\par percent to 25.827 to the euro, just off an October low, and the\par leu was down 0.1 percent at 4.439.\par     The Polish zloty was flat while Hungary's forint\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  dipped 0.2 percent after outshining peers in earlier\par trade as investors welcomed government measures that go part of\par the way to unwinding the country's stock of foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par loans.\par     Hungary's ruling Fidesz party said on Monday that Hungary\par would use a temporary fix to help borrowers meet repayments on\par such loans, steering clear for the time being of action that\par could have hit the country's banks more drastically.\par  \par     "It looks good at first glance and will probably soothe\par tensions, although there is surely more to come at some point\par down the line," a dealer said in Budapest.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Stocks in Budapest rose 0.2 percent.\par     The Prague stock index underperformed as shares of\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telefonica Czech Republic\f28 \uc2 \f2  fell nearly 2 percent, nearer the\par purchase price paid by investment group PFF. \par     Spain's Telefonica is selling a 65.9 percent stake in its\par Czech at 305.60 crowns a share to investment group\par PPF, owned by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petr Kellner\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the Czech Republic's richest man and\par ranked at 106 in Forbes' list of the world's wealthiest people.\par                   CEE MARKETS SNAPSHOT AT 1515 CET\par  ************************** \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \hig