\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-\uc2 Czech  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  to avoid crown  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  for now\b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2013\par 16:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 PRAGUE, Sept 23 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't opt to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it meets on Thursday but the possibility is not likely to disappear in the coming months, according to a Reuters poll.\par \par \uc2 With the Czech key two-week repo rate at 0.05 percent since November, the bank has been considering weakening the crown as a policy tool to aid recovery in an economy just getting out of a record recession.\par \par \uc2 Fifteen of 18 analysts polled by Reuters between Sept. 16-23 expect rate setters to opt against \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this month. Three analysts did not answer.\par \par \uc2 While the Czech economy has just emerged from its longest-ever period of contraction, analysts say low inflation and a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has stayed resilient to a selloff in emerging markets since the summer will keep the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alive.\par \par \uc2 "Although CPI growth fell further in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Czech Republic\b0 \highlight\uc2 , expected recovery in the euro zone should ease the pressure to launch \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Tomas Holinka, analyst with \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Analytics.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (CNB) formally voted on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at its last meeting in August but decided against stepping into the market, which would be its first such move in over a decade.\par \par \uc2 The bank will release new economic forecasts in November.\par \par \uc2 "We think that the hawks are likely still in a mild majority. Hence, the new November forecast likely has to persuade them," Jaromir Sindel, Citibank's chief economist in Prague, said.\par \par \uc2 As trade with the euro zone faltered and consumers held back spending while facing job uncertainty, central Europe's policymakers have slashed interest rates in the past year.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would help prop up price growth by making imports more expensive, enticing people to spend now. A weaker crown would also help exporters, raising their income and bringing more money into the economy.\par \par \uc2 But it carries risks and could even backfire by depressing consumer demand. (Reporting by Mirka Krufova and Jason Hovet; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 CZECH-RATES/  (POLL) | ABN | M | E | RBN | D | CZS   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130926e99n000rz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
