\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ Blog:\uc2 Czech  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  on the Fence about  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 658 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 2013\par 15:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (This story has been posted on The Wall Street Journal Online's Emerging Europe blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 By Sean Carney\par \par \uc2 The longest-ever Czech recession continues unabated as fresh data Monday showed export growth weakening and industrial output contracting, but still hasn't tipped the balance of opinion towards \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the koruna.\par \par \uc2 "The monetary policy board has seven members and only three members want immediate action. It's going to be difficult to convince the fourth. \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are costly for the bank and the outlook is very uncertain, " said economist Vladim\u237\'00\'EDr Pikora at Nextfinance in Prague.\par \par \uc2 The indicators Monday showed that imports and exports are falling even though the country enjoys a foreign trade surplus, suggesting that domestic and foreign demand are weak.\par \par \uc2 This comes as inflation decreased 0.4 percentage point to 1.3% in May from April, well below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2% target.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which last year cut its benchmark interest rate to 0.05%, believes that overall risks to the economy are disinflationary and "tilted to a need for easier monetary conditions," according to minutes from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's June 27 policy meeting, also released Monday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the data strengthen the disinflationary trend that it noted six weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 "The board members also agreed that the need to further ease the monetary conditions had increased compared to the situation" in mid-May, the minutes said.\par \par \uc2 But launching an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still a hotly contested topic on the seven-member monetary policy board.\par \par \uc2 "Several board members spoke in favor of immediately commencing \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, it was also said that the tendency to undershoot the inflation target was only short term in nature and that a necessary condition for commencing \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a risk of sustained deflation, which was not materialising," the minutes said.\par \par \uc2 Elements that make a potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  more likely include the \b \highlight22\uc2 Czech Republic\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current political uncertainty, which may prevent fiscal policy from easing as was expected, so "monetary policy would have to take this into account" the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 It said the scope of potential \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "unlimited," adding that a weaker koruna would impact the economy more quickly than interest rate changes.\par \par \uc2 There are several factors working against an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , namely the koruna is trading against the euro at a weaker level than the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  forecasts.\par \par \uc2 "It's entirely possible that the remainder of the [monetary policy] board is quietly betting that euro-zone developments will work on behalf of the \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and market developments themselves will weaken the koruna," Nextfinance's Mr. Pikora said.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, the tendency to undershoot the inflation target "was only short term in nature and that a necessary condition for commencing \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a risk of sustained deflation, which was not materialising," the minutes said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also noted that the current improvement in German consumer confidence offered hope that a turnaround in external demand for Czech goods might materialise.\par \par \uc2 Citfin analyst Jiri Simek said Monday's economic indicators aren't great but can be seen as part of a larger picture over which local monetary policy has little influence.\par \par \uc2 Industrial output declined in May largely due to the country's mining sector posting an annual production decrease of more than 25% in the month, but that was mainly because of record-low coal prices.\par \par \uc2 An annual decline in automobile sales in May followed a surge the previous month.\par \par \uc2 "I wouldn't view these numbers so tragically. For the whole year, industrial output growth should be about zero, it's not going to have a major impact on the economy," Mr. Simek said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Sean Carney at sean.carney@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  For continuously updated news from The Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 \f2 . \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 08-07-13 1352GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130708e978000hq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
