\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 2-Hungarian bonds retreat, CEE  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  mixed\b0\par\par\uc2 854 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2013\par 17:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Investors switch into Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  mixed, flow into Romanian bonds lifts leu\par \par \uc2 * Attention turning to \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting\par \par \uc2 By Jason Hovet and Sandor Peto\par \par \uc2 PRAGUE/BUDAPEST, April 26 (Reuters) - Forint-denominated Hungarian government bonds retreated on Friday as investors continued to shift into foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt following a decline in domestic yields.\par \par \uc2 Investors globally are seeking higher yields offered by emerging market assets relative to developed markets. In Romania, domestic debt as well as foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt is in demand, due to still high yields, and demand for Romanian paper on Friday lifted the leu.\par \par \uc2 Central European policymakers have been cutting interest rates to help their economies fight recession or economic slowdown, but yields are still mostly attractive.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut its base rate nine times, each by a quarter percentage point, since August to 4.75 percent.\par \par \uc2 Markets have priced in further cuts to 3.50 percent, pushing yields on forint-denominated bonds to record lows in the past few weeks and below yields on euro- and dollar-denominated bonds. Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond yields would normally be lower as forint bonds usually include a yield premium to cover foreign investors' exchange rate risk.\par \par \uc2 "Many local funds have now switched to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds (in the past few days), and in linked derivatives deals investors can get an additional yield premium," a Budapest-based fixed income trader said.\par \par \uc2 "The yields on 10-year dollar bonds have come down (in recent days) to near 5 percent from 5.5, while the 10-year forint bond yield rose to 5.45 percent from 5.3 percent," the trader said.\par \par \uc2 In the Czech Republic, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already cut rates to near zero, the yield on 10-year eurobonds\par \par \uc2 fell to record lows below 2 percent.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region were mixed, with the Czech crown\par \par \uc2 firming 0.2 percent and the Romanian leu gaining 0.1 percent against the euro by 1444 GMT. The forint\par \par \uc2 eased 0.4 percent and the Polish zloty shed 0.2 percent.\par \par \uc2 Weak data from the region and from main trading partner Germany, along with cuts in interest rates, have weighed on the regions' \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past few months.\par \par \uc2 Romania, though, has resisted cutting rates to boost its slumping economy because of nagging concerns over inflation, and strong demand for the country's bonds after they were included in regional indices has underpinned its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It seems like another day of gains for the leu, and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  agents don't seem to be on the bid side noticeably," said a dealer in Bucharest. "The main support is still the longer-term trend of flows into bonds."\par \par \uc2 Yields on Romanian 10-year bonds fell 58 basis points at an auction on Thursday, boosting the leu.\par \par \uc2 In Czech markets, attention was turning to a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting next week.\par \par \uc2 Analysts in a Reuters poll on Thursday said the crown's losses over recent weeks had eliminated the chance of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepping in to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for now as a way of easing monetary conditions.\par \par \uc2 With interest rates already at 0.05 percent, the bank has been toying with the idea of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its battle with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Czech Republic\b0 \highlight\uc2 's longest recession in two decades.\par \par \uc2 The crown touched its lowest since November 2011 this week.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                    close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                             change   change\par                                             today    in 2013 \par Czech crown                  25.716    25.765  +0.19%    -2.6%\par Polish zloty                 4.157    4.15   -0.17%    -2%\par Hungarian forint             301.71    300.62   -0.36%    -3.56%\par Croatian kuna                7.594    7.603  +0.12%    -0.57%\par Romanian leu                 4.339    4.344  +0.12%   +2.4%\par Serbian dinar                110.61    110.89  +0.25%   +1.53%\par Yield Spreads\par Czech treasury bonds           \par 2-yr T-bond   CZ2YT=RR   +9 basis points to  37bps over bmk*\par 7-yr T-bond   CZ7YT=RR    0 basis points to  +66bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   CZ9YT=RR   +2 basis points to  +110bps over bmk*\par Hungarian treasury bonds           \par 3-yr T-bond   HU3YT=RR   +3 basis points to  +532bps over bmk*\par 5-yr T-bond   HU5YT=RR   +6 basis points to  +547bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   HU10YT=RR +11 basis points to  +512bps over bmk*\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Benchmark is German bond equivalent.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All data taken from Reuters at 1644 CET.\f28 \par \par 