\par\par \b \uc2 Czech c.banker says  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  not required -Bloomberg\b0\par\par\uc2 167 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 April 2013\par 08:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 PRAGUE, April 24 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Czech Republic\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not face a deflation threat that would require \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease monetary policy further, Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member \uc2 Pavel Rezabek\uc2  was quoted as saying on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut interest rates to near zero last year and said it would step into markets to weaken the crown against the euro if it needs to ease further.\par \par \uc2 Rezabek said in an interview with Bloomberg that the primary goal of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if conducted, would be to "solve a deflation problem".\par \par \uc2 "The risk of deflation has significantly declined, and we can say it may have even been fully eliminated, unless a major shock occurs," Rezabek was quoted as saying. "We should be careful about using this instrument as long as inflation on the policy horizon isn't at risk."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Jason Hovet; Editing by Catherine Evans)\par \par \uc2 CZECH-CBANKER/ (URGENT) | CZS | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | RNP | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130424e94o0007e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
