\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Czech c.bank minutes: risks to economic forecast point to easier policy\b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2013\par 09:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds background, details)\par \par \uc2 PRAGUE, April 5 (Reuters) - A majority of \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policymakers agreed that risks to the bank's economic forecast pointed to the need for lightly looser policy, minutes of their March meeting showed, highlighting the likelihood the bank could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the crown.\par \par \uc2 With the key two-week repo rate at 0.05 percent, a level the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  calls "a technical zero", policymakers have said they would not cut it any more and would use \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  if there is a need to relax policy further.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor \uc2 Miroslav Singer\uc2  said after the March 28 meeting that risks were skewed to the downside, which would indicate a need for loosening. However, the crown has weakened since then, partly due to the Cyprus crisis, dampening the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Czech Republic\b0 \highlight\uc2  is mired in its longest recession in two decades, worsened by a budget squeeze by the centre-right government which has hit consumption and prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut interest rates to near zero.\par \par \uc2 The point was raised at the March 28 policy meeting that domestic economic activity was more subdued than forecast and was anti-inflationary, the minutes of showed on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The economy shrank for a fourth straight quarter in the final three months of 2012 and by more than the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  forecast, while inflation stood at 1.7 percent in February, below the bank's outlook for 2.0 percent, which is also its target rate.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers pointed out repeatedly at the March meeting that directly influencing the exchange rate was an effective instrument in a small and open economy where policy rates are at zero.\par \par \uc2 However, the minutes showed that opinion among the seven members of the governing board was split on the effect of potential \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some argued that any \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the crown would raise prices of imported goods, which would prompt people to spend now rather than put off purchases on expectations prices would fall.\par \par \uc2 But it was also argued that a weaker crown would raise prices of "less elastic" items in the consumer basket such as food and energy, which might conversely depress aggregate consumption.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Jana Mlcochova; Editing by Susan Fenton)\par \par \uc2 CZECH-CBANK/MINUTES  (UPDATE 1) | CZS | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | RNP | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130405e945000bx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
