\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 2- \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  and stocks slip, leu close to high\b0\par\par\uc2 915 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2012\par 14:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Prospect of U.S. fiscal crunch pressures assets\par \par \uc2 * Romanian leu, stocks still close to highs after election\par \par \uc2 By Jason Hovet and Sam Cage\par \par \uc2 PRAGUE/BUCHAREST, Dec 28 (Reuters) - C entral European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  a nd stocks were a touch lower on Friday as U.S. lawmakers sought to avoid an end of year f iscal crunch, while Rom ania's leu a n d stocks rem ained close to sev en-month highs due to increased political stability.\par \par \uc2 Stock markets in central Europe fell up to 0.5 percent - though the Warsaw bourse was close to its highest since mid-2011.\par \par \uc2 Bonds were flat, with Polish yields close to record lows after Warsaw said it planned to have more than half its 2013 financing needs covered after the first quarter.\par \par \uc2 Investors were eyeing last-minute efforts by U.S. officials to reach a deal that would avoid some $600 billion in tax hikes and spending cuts due to kick in at the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 Few analysts predict a deal that will deal with all the issues dividing Republicans and Democrats at once but many have tempered concern by speculating the government will muddle through and find deals that can ease some of the worst of the impact on the economy.\par \par \uc2 "In general, the market seems to be positive and expectant with regards to the U.S. solution, though (market) volatility is likely to prevail until the very last moment," a dealer in Budapest said.\par \par \uc2 The R omania n leu is the region's worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  i n a year which has seen it flick between f our governments, preventing th e \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from following its peers and cutting rates to support growth.\par \par \uc2 The leu slipped 0.2 percent to 4.435 per euro by 1251 GMT , b ut remained c lose to a seven-month high hit after a new government took office following a convincing election win. The Bucharest bourse hit its highest since May. [ID: nL5E8NL3KG]\par \par \uc2 "We see the RON caught in the 4.42-4.44 per euro range for this year's last couple of sessions," said ING analyst Mihai Tantaru.\par \par \uc2 COOLING MARKET\par \par \uc2 The forint and zloty have led gains in emerging Europe this year with r ises of 8.1 percent and 9.5 percent respectively, as their higher yields attracted investors in a rally fuelled by major global central banks' liquidity-boosting measures.\par \par \uc2 Easing monetary policy in the region has cooled the market in the last half of 2012, though, causing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to mostly flatten out going into 2013.\par \par \uc2 The Hungarian forint dropped to its lowest level versus the euro since June this week while the local market was closed for a holiday, but it has regained about half those losses.\par \par \uc2 T he forint inched up 0. 2 percent to 29 0.8 to the euro, after reaching a low of 295.5 on Wednesday. P oland's zloty\par \par \uc2 was down 0. 3 percent a t 4.079 .\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 Czech Republic\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the crown could be the next monetary easing tool now that rates are near zero. Dealers have said the level of 25 to the euro could be decisive for the bank.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has gained nearly 2 percent this year, w as 0 .3 percent lower at 25.119 t o the euro.\par \par \uc2 "There is not much power to push the crown below 25," a Prague \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                    close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                             change   change\par                                             today    in 2012 \par Czech crown                  25.119    25.057   -0.25%   +1.7%\par Polish zloty                 4.079    4.066   -0.32%   +9.46%\par Hungarian forint             290.8    291.43  +0.22%   +8.18%\par Croatian kuna                7.548    7.555  +0.09%    -0.43%\par Romanian leu                 4.435    4.427   -0.18%    -2.57%\par Serbian dinar                113.49    113.77  +0.25%    -5.76%\par Yield Spreads\par Czech treasury bonds           \par 2-yr T-bond   CZ2YT=RR    -4 basis points to  44bps over bmk*\par 7-yr T-bond   CZ6YT=RR   +1 basis points to  +56bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   CZ10YT=RR   +4 basis points to  +59bps over bmk*\par Polish treasury bonds           \par 2-yr T-bond   PL2YT=RR    -2 basis points to  +307bps over bmk*\par 5-yr T-bond   PL5YT=RR   +3 basis points to  +286bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond PL10YT=RR   +4 basis points to  +240bps over bmk*\par Hungarian treasury bonds           \par 3-yr T-bond   HU3YT=RR    -3 basis points to  +552bps over bmk*\par 5-yr T-bond   HU5YT=RR   +2 basis points to  +555bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   HU10YT=RR  0 basis points to  +475bps over bmk*\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Benchmark is German bond equivalent.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All data taken from Reuters at 1351 CET.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  percent change calculated from the daily domestic\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 close at 1600 GMT.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For related news and prices, click on the code