\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING: Hungarian Inflation Set to Slow in November\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sean Carney   \par \uc2 829 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2012\par 04:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \par Local/GMT \par 0900/0800 Hungary November CPI \par 0900/0800 Hungary minister, central banker speak at conference \par 1130/1030 Hungary 3-month T-bill auction \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hungary's economy and monetary policy will be the focus of investors' attention Tuesday, with a slowdown in inflation expected.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Consumer price inflation is set to slow to 5.5% in November from 6% in October and an annual peak of 6.6% in September; this is mainly because of a drop in fuel prices that offset a rise in food costs, Erste Bank analysts said. Increases in excise tax rises this time last year also boosted CPI then.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's dovish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate setter Andrea Bartfai-Mager and the country's envoy for credit-line talks with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 , Mihaly Varga, will speak at a conference organized by business daily Vilaggazdasag.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Bartfai-Mager will focus on monetary policy and rates in her speech, after having been part of the slight majority that has cut Hungary's key rate by 0.25 percentage point each time since August to 6%.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Varga will speak about the Hungary's financing, most likely adding new details about the status of the government's talks with the \uc2 European Union\uc2  and the IMF, which came to a standstill at the end of October.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par EUR/CZK \par Latest 0250 GMT 25.244-82 \par Previous 2150 GMT 25.246-303 \par %Chg -0.04 \par  \par EUR/HUF \par Latest 0250 GMT 283.04-64 \par Previous 2150 GMT 283.25-71 \par % Chg -0.05 \par  \par EUR/PLN \par Latest 0250 GMT 4.1040-114 \par Previous 2150 GMT 4.1055-123 \par % Chg -0.03 \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par Hungary \par         Mon    Fri \par 3 yrs   5.77%  5.83% \par 5 yrs   6.15%  6.20% \par 10yrs   6.50%  6.64% \par  \par Poland \par         Mon    Fri \par 3 yrs   3.22%  3.32(1) \par 5 yrs   3.26%  3.34% \par 10yrs   3.71%  3.83% \par (1) 2 yrs \par  \par Czech Republic \par         Mon    Fri \par 3 yrs   0.20%  0.21% \par 5 yrs   0.73%  0.77% \par 10yrs   1.90%  1.90% \par  \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG 20 \par 2,476.53 +25.79 +1.05% \par  \par BUX \par 17,744.29 -40.77 -0.23% \par  \par PX \par 985.84 -7.68 -0.77% \par  \par EU Enlarged \par 1,918.16 +15.67 +0.82% \par  \par OTHER NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: The Polish economy would benefit from a stable or slightly stronger zloty as it would lower import prices and reduce the financial burden on the many Poles who have foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  mortgages, Andrzej Bratkowski, a member of the country's monetary policy council, told DJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Trader Monday.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CZECH REPUBLIC\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the koruna may come in mid-2013 and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's near-zero interest rates may remain until late 2014 as no inflationary pressures can be seen, a central banker said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In an interview, Lubomir Lizal, a member of the bank's monetary policy board, said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's record-low benchmark interest rate of 0.05% will remain in place until inflationary pressures emerge. When asked if he sees any inflationary risks at present, he simply said "no."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Hungary's austerity steps to further inhibit growth as they comprise additional tax increases, says Renaissance Capital. Despite a deteriorating inflation outlook and associated HUF risks, market expectations are for further policy rate cuts "to be pushed by the external members of the Monetary Policy Council, backed by the ruling Fidesz party," bringing the policy rate down by 50-75bps by the end of next year from the current 6.00%, it adds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Hungary can't get out of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Excessive Deficit Procedure next year unless the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts its forecast of the country's 2014 budget deficit by the middle of 2013 to less than 3% of economic output, Economy Minister Gyorgy Matolcsy said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: Romania's electoral office announced on Monday that two regional referendums on gold mine and shale gas projects were invalidated a day after too few people turned out to vote.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The referendums Sunday, which failed to meet the 50% turnout threshold, were held alongside general elections that saw the center-left ruling coalition win a landslide victory.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: Romania's governing coalition comfortably won a weekend parliamentary poll, partial results showed Monday, in an outcome likely to fuel tensions that have raised concern over the democratic credentials of the country.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Social-Liberal Union, or USL, headed by Prime Minister Victor Ponta took nearly 60% of the vote, according to results from more than four-fifths of polling stations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Veronika Gulyas in Budapest contributed to this briefing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sean Carney\f28 \uc2 \f2  at sean.carney@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe}}}\uc2 \f2  for the new Dow Jones blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region. [ 12-10-12 2218ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020121211e8cb0000n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
