\par\par \b \uc2 CNB-Czech Central Banker Lizal Sees No Inflationary Pressures\b0\par\par\uc2 602 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2012\par \uc2 ENP Newswire\par \uc2 ENPNEW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012, Electronic News Publishing. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 Release date - 10122012\par \par \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the koruna may come in mid-2013 and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s near-zero interest rates may remain until late 2014 as no inflationary pressures can be seen, a central banker said Monday.\par \par \uc2 In an interview, Lubomir Lizal, a member of the bank\u8217\'20\'19s monetary policy board, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s record-low benchmark interest rate of 0.05% will remain in place until inflationary pressures emerge.\par \par \uc2 When asked if he sees any inflationary risks at present, he simply said \u8216\'20\'18no.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 When asked how long rates can remain near zero, he said \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19d rather target conditions and not periods of time.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s own forecasts, which span a period of 18 months, there are no indications of any rising pressures on consumer prices, he said.\par \par \uc2 The country\u8217\'20\'19s headline inflation rate was above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 1% to 3% target range in the first 10 months of the year, but that was largely due to increases in value-added taxes that took effect in January.\par \par \uc2 Monetary policy-relevant inflation, which looks at prices that can be influenced by monetary policy, has been in the lower end of the target inflation range all year, taking pressure off rate-setters.\par \par \uc2 The Czech economy has been in recession since late 2011, as domestic demand tumbled amid falling real wages, tax hike-fueled inflation, rising unemployment, government spending cuts and negative fallout from the euro zone\u8217\'20\'19s many crises.\par \par \uc2 As a result the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has largely exhausted its standard monetary toolbox centered on interest rates and now is considering how to further ease monetary conditions if the need should arise.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Lizal said that now that interest rates are close to zero, \u8216\'20\'18the natural question is what\u8217\'20\'19s next. For a small, open economy like the \b \highlight22\uc2 Czech Republic\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in current conditions \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is the best second tool you have.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not considering other non-standard monetary tools such as quantitative easing, as the Czech financial system already enjoys a surplus of liquidity and putting more money into the system would not help.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Lizal said he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t favor a particular \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate for the koruna, but rather will gauge policy needs via inflation, economic performance and current market developments.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Based on the latest prognosis from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it suggests further monetary easing in the middle of next year,\u8217\'20\'19 Mr. Lizal said, adding that the bank\u8217\'20\'19s forecasts have been largely accurate in the recent past and so he is comfortable with this estimation.\par \par \uc2 The discussion now is about the tool to use, not how and when to use it, he said without directly responding to a question on what \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate he\u8217\'20\'19d like to see.\par \par \uc2 On Oct. 19, Kamil Janacek, Mr. Lizal\u8217\'20\'19s peer on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s seven-strong monetary policy board, said an exchange rate of above 25 koruna to the euro is good for exporters and the economy and is the strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate he\u8217\'20\'19d like to see so long as the economy is weak.\par \par \uc2 At 1402 GMT Monday, the koruna traded at 25.25 to the euro. The koruna has remained above 25 to the euro since late October.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Lizal also said any recovery by the Czech export-based economy hinges on a return to growth in the euro zone, which is the Czech Republic\u8217\'20\'19s largest trading partner.\par \par \uc2 [Editorial queries for this story should be sent to newswire@enpublishing.co.uk]\par \par \uc2 Dokument ENPNEW0020121211e8cb0005x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
