\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING: Hungarian Inflation Set to Slow in November\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sean Carney   \par \uc2 829 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2012\par 04:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \par Local/GMT \par 0900/0800 Hungary November CPI \par 0900/0800 Hungary minister, central banker speak at conference \par 1130/1030 Hungary 3-month T-bill auction \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hungary's economy and monetary policy will be the focus of investors' attention Tuesday, with a slowdown in inflation expected.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Consumer price inflation is set to slow to 5.5% in November from 6% in October and an annual peak of 6.6% in September; this is mainly because of a drop in fuel prices that offset a rise in food costs, Erste Bank analysts said. Increases in excise tax rises this time last year also boosted CPI then.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's dovish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate setter Andrea Bartfai-Mager and the country's envoy for credit-line talks with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 , Mihaly Varga, will speak at a conference organized by business daily Vilaggazdasag.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Bartfai-Mager will focus on monetary policy and rates in her speech, after having been part of the slight majority that has cut Hungary's key rate by 0.25 percentage point each time since August to 6%.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Varga will speak about the Hungary's financing, most likely adding new details about the status of the government's talks with the \uc2 European Union\uc2  and the IMF, which came to a standstill at the end of October.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par EUR/CZK \par Latest 0250 GMT 25.244-82 \par Previous 2150 GMT 25.246-303 \par %Chg -0.04 \par  \par EUR/HUF \par Latest 0250 GMT 283.04-64 \par Previous 2150 GMT 283.25-71 \