 austerity steps to further inhibit growth as they comprise additional tax increases, says Renaissance Capital. Despite a deteriorating inflation outlook and associated HUF risks, market expectations are for further policy rate cuts "to be pushed by the external members of the Monetary Policy Council, backed by the ruling Fidesz party," bringing the policy rate down by 50-75bps by the end of next year from the current 6.00%, it adds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Hungary can't get out of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Excessive Deficit Procedure next year unless the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts its forecast of the country's 2014 budget deficit by the middle of 2013 to less than 3% of economic output, Economy Minister Gyorgy Matolcsy said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: Romania's electoral office announced on Monday that two regional referendums on gold mine and shale gas projects were invalidated a day after too few people turned out to vote.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The referendums Sunday, which failed to meet the 50% turnout threshold, were held alongside general elections that saw the center-left ruling coalition win a landslide victory.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: Romania's governing coalition comfortably won a weekend parliamentary poll, partial results showed Monday, in an outcome likely to fuel tensions that have raised concern over the democratic credentials of the country.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Social-Liberal Union, or USL, headed by Prime Minister Victor Ponta took nearly 60% of the vote, according to results from more than four-fifths of polling stations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Veronika Gulyas in Budapest contributed to this briefing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sean Carney\f28 \uc2 \f2  at sean.carney@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe}}}\uc2 \f2  for t