\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Czech c.banker: no need for QE,  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  possible\b0\par\par\uc2 363 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2012\par 10:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quote, background)\par \par \uc2 PRAGUE, Nov 20 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Czech Republic\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not need quantitative easing but that does not stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from considering market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the crown, the bank's Vice-Governor Mojmir Hampl said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The bank has said \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be the next tool if it needs to relax policy further after cutting its main repo rate to 0.05 percent this month.\par \par \uc2 Governor \uc2 Miroslav Singer\uc2  has said there may be a need to ease policy more around the middle of 2013.\par \par \uc2 "When my colleague Singer says something about possible entry into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, let me remind you that this is not a thought about this market, this economy needing some liquidity injections," Hampl told an economic seminar.\par \par \uc2 "This is in a situation when you cannot go below zero in interest rates and you have the feeling that there are anti-inflationary risks, you will not meet the inflation target, then one of the first tools that comes into mind is the exchange rate, with all the risks that it entails."\par \par \uc2 Hampl's six-year term runs out in December but he may be reappointed for another one.\par \par \uc2 He has repeatedly spoken against non-standard policies, such as the quantitative easing employed in the United States and Britain to pump money into the economy, saying the economy was fundamentally sound and did not need it.\par \par \uc2 An \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the crown would increase the local value of exporters' earnings. Price rises caused by a weaker exchange rate would also help the bank bring inflation up towards its 2 percent target.\par \par \uc2 The crown traded at 25.270 to the euro on Tuesday. It has lost 3.4 percent since Singer began talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  or other easing tools, compared to a 0.9 percent weakening of the Polish zloty and the Romanian leu\par \par \uc2 and a 0.4 percent firming of the Hungarian forint\par \par \uc2 in the same period.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Robert Mueller; writing by Jan Lopatka; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 CZECH-CBANK/  (UPDATE 1) | CZS | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | RNP | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121120e8bk000ga\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
