\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Czech Central Banker Singer: Exports Outlook Poor through Year-End\b0\par\par\uc2 434 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 November 2012\par 13:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 15 Nov 2012 07:45 EDT *DJ  Czech Central Banker: Exporters Face Demand Drop in Euro Area\par \par \uc2 15 Nov 2012 07:54 EDT *DJ  Czech Central Banker: \b \highlight22\uc2 FX Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  Remain Policy Tools for Now\par \par \uc2 15 Nov 2012 08:09 EDT *DJ  Czech Central Banker: Tame Price Pressures Warrant Easy Monetary Policy\par \par \uc2 15 Nov 2012 08:10 EDT *DJ  Czech Central Banker: Looser Monetary Policy Needed through Mid-2013\par \par \uc2 15 Nov 2012 08:49 EDT DJ  Czech Central Banker: \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Key Policy Tool\par \par \uc2 By Leos Rousek\par \par \uc2 TRUTNOV, \b \highlight22\uc2 Czech Republic\b0 \highlight\uc2 --The \uc2 Czech National Bank\uc2  will focus on using \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the koruna weak, as the outlook for Czech exports remains poor due to recession in the euro area, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market remains our key policy channel," Miroslav Singer told the annual conference of the country's Exporters' Association held in Trutnov, north-east of Prague.\par \par \uc2 Two weeks ago the CNB lowered its headline interest to 0.05% and said that after bringing the rate to nearly zero it may use the exchange rate as its main policy tool. By weakening the koruna Czech goods and services may be priced more cheaply on foreign markets and help local exporters.\par \par \uc2 "Price pressures remain tame, which warrants looser monetary policies," Mr. Singer said. "The looser policy may be needed until about the middle of the next year."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Singer declined to specify an adequate exchange rate of the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the euro. However, he described the current koruna levels at above 25.00 against the euro as weak.\par \par \uc2 Czech exporters will continue to face strong head winds at least through the rest of the year, Mr. Singer said.\par \par \uc2 The Czech economy contracted 0.3% in the three months through end-September against the previous quarter, intensifying its recession. The country's gross domestic product has been contracting for five consecutive quarter, the longest economic slump since its previous deep recession in 1996-97.\par \par \uc2 Declines in consumer spending, weighed by the growing unemployment and declining real disposable incomes, were the main driver of the GDP slide, while easing net exports were no longer able to offset the poor domestic demand.\par \par \uc2 Write to Leos Rousek at leos.rousek@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Go to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope }}}\uc2  for the new WSJ and Dow Jones blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 15, 2012 08:49 ET (13:49 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020121115e8bf003ns\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
