\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Nordea Sees Verbal  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Risk On Koruna\b0\par\par\uc2 1,236 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2011\par 11:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1059 GMT (Dow Jones) Nordea sees a risk of postponed rate hikes in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Czech Republic\b0 \highlight\uc2  or verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the koruna strengthens too fast. In the last two months, CZK has been one of the world's best-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the euro, notching gains of almost 6%, the bank says. Due to that fast appreciation, the bank says it's only "moderately positive" on the koruna in the short term. On a 3 and 6-month horizon, Nordea has revised down its EUR/CZK forecasts to CZK24 and CZK24.25, from CZK24.50 and CZK24.25 respectively. On a 12-month basis, Nordea has adjusted its EUR/CZK view down to CZK23.50 from CZK24.25. It currently trades at CZK23.997.(clare.connaghan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par +44-20-7842-9464; markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1058 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/PKR is lower at 85.26 from 85.54 late Monday, a level last touched on June 10; a Pakistan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman confirms the pair is near a nine-month low. A dealer with a state-run bank says the pair is lower, mirroring regional weakness in the greenback and a lack of importer bids. He adds, remittance inflows from overseas Pakistanis and exporters selling the USD pushed the pair lower, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. The dealer says a weaker USD may encourage buying on dips in coming trading sessions. He tips the pair in a 85.25-85.35 band Wednesday. (djn.in@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1055 GMT [Dow Jones] Indian government bonds are higher on improving liquidity and a retreat in crude oil prices on signs of easing political upheaval in Egypt, says a dealer with a state-run bank. The most-traded 8.13% 2022 bond is at 99.24 from 99.14 at Monday's close. "The upside in bond prices was limited due to a mid-term view on India's inflation and a rate hike by China. Besides, bonds are drawing comfort from an immediate betterment of liquidity," the dealer says. Borrowing on the RBI's liquidity auction window has fallen to a daily average of INR500 billion-INR700 billion from over INR1 trillion in the October-December quarter. He tips the 12-year paper yield in a 8.20%-8.25% range in the near-term, currently at 8.23%. China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Tuesday raised interest rates by 25 bps. (sourav.mishra@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1054 GMT (Dow Jones) EUR/USD breaks through the day's high of 1.3650, triggers stops, some likely option related, and pushes on to the day's high of 1.3666. That move helps the euro on the crosses with EUR/CHF at 1.3037, EUR/GBP 0.8467 and EUR/JPY at 112.22, all at the day's highs. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1044 GMT (Dow Jones) Peripheral euro-zone bund spreads are steady around Tuesday's slightly wider opening levels. Ireland's 10-year spreads are up 5 bps at 552 bps, Portugal's up 3 bps at 384, and Spain's up 2 bps at 187, according to Tradeweb. "We're a little bit weaker, but things are quiet and peripherals are waiting for direction from the core rates market, and whether than can head lower or rally." (mark.brown@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1041 GMT (Dow Jones) The USD firms pretty much across the board after the PBOC hikes rates by 25 bps but then surrenders that move. EUR/USD sheds around 20 ticks to 1.3620 but bounces back to 1.3640 almost immediately. GBP/USD falls by the same margin with a less pronounced bounce; now at 1.6122. AUD/USD sheds 50 ticks to the session low of 1.0139; now at 1.0155. USD/JPY barely budged and trades at 82.13. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1039 GMT (Dow Jones) The major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs are holding within the day's ranges in a lackluster session. EUR/USD peaked at 1.3650 in early Europe, slipped under 1.36 and is now back up at 1.3634. GBP/USD ran into strong selling interest around 1.6160, dipped to 1.6087 but is now back up at 1.6127. USD/JPY found bids on its dip to 82.00 while AUD/USD is running into offers ahead of 1.02. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1032 GMT [Dow Jones] U.S. Treasurys are moving in tandem with bunds on Tuesday with the March U.S. Treasury contract 20 ticks higher at 118.215. There were small losses in the short-end and minor gains in the long-end of the curve at the close in U.S. trading while selling of the belly of the curve was seen in Asian hours. Supply is the key theme for the market in the short-term with Tuesday seeing the start of the latest round of refunding with USD32 billion of 3-years on the block. The 2-year US Treasury currently yields 0.76%, the 5-year yields 2.275% and the 10-year yields 3.645%. (nick.cawley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1031 GMT (Dow Jones) EUR/USD's setback to 1.35 found buying interest as expected and it should now head back to the range highs of 1.3865 followed by 1.40 and then 1.4185 says \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 . On the downside an unexpected break below 1.35 would suggest weakness is more than just a correction, and open risk toward the 1.32 area says the bank. EUR/USD now at 1.3618. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par +44-20-7842-9464; markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1028 GMT [Dow Jones] Open interest in the futures market can be a good indicator of whether the recent bout of higher German bond yields is due to the setting of new short positions or liquidation of existing longs, says Credit Agricole. The bank says there is currently a positive correlation between the recent fall in the price of bunds and the fall in open interest, indicating the liquidation of long positions. The picture in the bobl contract, however, shows a negative correlation, with open interest increasing as the price falls, indicating the establishing of new shorts. (nick.cawley@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par +44-20-7842-9464; markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1027 GMT [Dow Jones] The UKT 2022 linker offers value in both forward real yield and forward breakeven vs the 2017 linker, and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2  recommends holders of the shorter-dated issue to use Tuesday's GBP1B tap to extend on the curve. The gilt is also relatively cheap in asset-swap terms compared to nearby linkers as well as the nominal curve, BarCap adds.(neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par +44-20-7842-9464; markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1025 GMT (Dow Jones) Switzerland's January consumer price index is expected to have risen 0.5% on the year, according to the average of estimates from five economists canvassed by Dow Jones Newswires. On the month, consumer prices are seen as likely to have slipped 0.3%. The data are due for release Thursday at 0815 GMT.(neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par +44-20-7842-9464; markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 02-08-11 0559ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110208e7280006x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
