\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:CEE BRIEFING:  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Seen Weak, Equities Mixed\b0\par\par\uc2 976 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 08:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds trader comment to Russian opening stock call)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Sean Carney \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \par    TODAY'S CALENDAR \par  \par    Local/GMT \par  \par    1000/0700 Meeting of Russia's State Duma \par    1800/1700 Poland's software company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asseco Poland SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  releases 2009, 4Q earnings \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Trading in equities and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in central Europe Friday may be volatile despite a lackluster schedule of events.\par \par \uc2 A rally over the last two weeks has brought new six-month highs to Central Europe's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but analysts said the trend may run out of steam as investors take profits.\par \par \uc2 What's more, in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Czech Republic\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in coming days if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rally continues as it would threaten the country's export competitiveness, bank \uc2 Ceska Sporitelna\uc2  said in a note.\par \par \uc2 In equity markets, Czech power company \uc2 CEZ AS\uc2  (BAACEZ.PR) may see volatile trade Friday due to the news late-Thursday that a sought after upgrade of its largest coal-fired power plant still faces challenges.\par \par \uc2 Czech Environment Minister Jan Dusik Thursday resigned after a disagreement with the prime minister over the issuance of environmental clearance for the renovation of CEZ's Prunerov power plant.\par \par \uc2 Dusik said he was unable to make the final ruling on the global environmental impact of the proposed revamp of the Prunerov power plant revamp as sought by CEZ while the Prime Minister wanted a final verdict.\par \par \uc2 In Warsaw, leading software integrator Assseco Poland SA (ACP.WA) is expected to report a slightly weaker set of numbers due to slower corporate demand and shrinking margins. The market will look for 2010 outlook, and in particular for signs of a revival in public sector demand.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par         Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par                    2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par EUR/CZK 25.3900-10 25.3720-20 +0.07  25.3980 25.3950  -3.79 \par EUR/HUF 262.13-64  261.98-49  +0.06  262.31  262.37   -3.12 \par EUR/PLN 3.8775-25  3.8782-02  -0.02  3.8777  3.8784   -5.55 \par USD/RUB 29.285-90  29.302-07  -0.06  29.319  29.287   -3.39 \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hungarian forint is seen hovering around current strong levels on favorable investor sentiment, a trader said, adding that the euro will likely trade between HUF262-HUF263.2 Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After a recent rally, the Polish zloty may be set for a corrective move Friday, with EUR/PLN bouncing toward the 3.8850 level, a local dealer said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Russian ruble, also having rallied, is likely to follow oil lower on profit-taking and a possible dip in oil prices, said a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader at Uralsib brokerage. "This will be a very short-term move lower, and not a violation of the current trend. I would continue to buy the ruble for the medium term."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Czech koruna may still have room to post more gains, but after rallying to a six-month high this week, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is likely to loose momentum ahead of Czech elections, scheduled for May, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ceska Sporitelna\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par HUNGARIAN BOND YIELDS--The three-year benchmark bond yield was 6.08% late Thursday from 6.13% Wednesday afternoon. The five-year was 6.38% from 6.41%, and the 10-year was 7.05% from 7.15%. \par  \par POLISH BOND YIELDS--The average yield on two-year paper was 4.65% compared with 4.67% late Wednesday, on five-year at 5.17% compared with 5.19%, on 10-year at 5.54% compared with 5.55%. \par  \par CZECH BOND YIELD--The yield on the benchmark 10-year paper was again unchanged on the day at 4.13% late Thursday. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Polish bonds may weaken slightly on Friday, mainly because the recent rally made them ripe for a correction, a local trader said. "But if so, I don't expect any major movements," he added. "Average yields shouldn't rise higher than by five basis points."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The current strengthening trend on the Hungarian treasury bond market will likely sustain, a trader said. The market is pricing a 5% key rate level, which indicates that there's room for further rate cuts after the elections, he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG20                    2445.40   loss   20.6    dn 0.8% \par BUX                     24000.01   gain  219.3    up 0.9% \par PX                       1208.5    loss    9.6    dn 0.8% \par RTS                      1558.8    loss    4.7    dn 0.3% \par MICEX                    1435.45   loss    1.9    dn 0.13% \par DJ Stoxx EU Enlarged 15  2632.1    loss    9.4    dn 0.4% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN WARSAW: The WIG20 is likely to face resistance to gains amid "a flat correction," a local broker said, listing lack of impulses as the main reason for a massive selloff. "If 2400 support is defended, then the index is likely to move toward 2500 level again," he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN PRAGUE: Trades in Czech stocks are likely to remain lackluster Friday. Unless the U.S. markets post some recovery, Czech blue-chips will probably keep heading lower, a local trader said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN BUDAPEST: Hungarian stocks could take a breather and remain stable Friday after trading up Thursday afternoon, an Erste Bank trader said. The market mood will nevertheless probably remain positive, which the trader expects to help keep share prices at current high levels.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN MOSCOW: Russian indices may fall up to 1.5% on profit-taking Friday, said Andrei Kuk, a senior trader at Uralsib. "Equities have had quite a run in the last few days, and traders are looking to lock in profits. Oil turning lower gives them an opportunity to do this." Market players may not find any strong reason to be either bullish or bearish today, as no vital economic statistics are expected and oil prices have stabilized in the $81 range, Olma brokerage said. [ 03-19-10 0334ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100319e63j0004d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
