\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-Czech cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to knock crown lower. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jan Lopatka \par \uc2 620 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2002\par 15:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  PRAGUE, April 4 (Reuters) - The Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday to weaken the bullish crown, making good on pledges to use heavy guns to prevent further sharp firming of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to record highs. \par \par \uc2  Traders estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought some 200-250 million euros for crowns to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had gained 14 percent over the past year on strong foreign direct investment inflows into the European Union candidate country. \par \par \uc2  The crown dropped to 30.67/70 to the euro from 30.31/34 before the bank started selling at around 30.35. It had the record high of 30.19 seen earlier in the session. \par \par \uc2  The drop took the crown 1.2 percent lover to levels last seen on Tuesday. Traders said the market believed the bank could return to take the crown further down. But analysts said the action would have a short-term impact, the crown's upward trend remains in place and the bank has little chance to achieve more than to slow it down. \par \par \uc2  "In the short run, if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming days, the crown could weaken over 31, but it is not possible for them to be in the market for too long," said David Marek, an analyst at Patria Finance. "Then the appreciation pressure will return," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came on the heels of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's warning earlier in the day that the crown's sharp firming in the past days - as much as 2.3 percent since last week - was creating a dangerous bubble. \par \par \uc2  "The CNB's board considers the present development (of the crown) as an exchange rate bubble. The CNB will reflect this evaluation in its further steps," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in an unusual written comment on the exchange rate ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Foreign manufacturers have been pouring into the \b \highlight22\uc2 Czech Republic\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the view of the country's joining the EU in about two years and the euro zone a few years later. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that the resulting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation was out of line with fundamentals and was threatening for the country's healthily growing economy. \par \par \uc2  "There is a deviation from a balanced development and an overshooting in the appreciation direction," the statement said. \par \par \uc2  "That leads to an excessive tightening of monetary conditions. This development may have a destabilising microeconomic and macroeconomic consequences." \par \par \uc2  The bank has repeatedly said it would like to see the crown appreciating at a slower pace, which would be in line with productivity gains in the economy which has been gradually catching up with richer neighbours to the west. \par \par \uc2  MARKET HAS UPPER HAND \par \par \uc2  The bank previously \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling crowns on the market in January, but the action had only a short-time effect. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  against domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is easier than supporting it, because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raises rather than depletes its hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, but still brings costs. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  loses money on the falling crown value of its reserves, and also on sterilising the crown cash it sells. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that this makes the bank relatively shy to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Huge inflows of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected as the result of the government's privatisation projects are lending further comfort that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is well sheltered, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has pledged to keep all the inflow off the market. \par \par \uc2  "It is possible they will come in again but they have no chance to pull (euro/crown) up... I don't think they can (weaken the crown to levels) above the 31.00-per-euro level," said one dealer at a Prague bank. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020404dy4400i85\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
