\par\par \b \uc2  Czech c.bank seen keeping rates flat at Thurs meet. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Klara Gajduskova \par \uc2 475 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2000\par 14:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  PRAGUE, April 26 (Reuters) - The Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (CNB) was likely to keep key interest rates unchanged at its monthly monetary policy meeting on Thursday after setting an ambitious end-2001 inflation target earlier in the week, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The market doubted the CNB would decide to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  again, following the bank's announcement of a net inflation goal of between 2.0 and 4.0 percent for December, 2001, analysts told Reuters on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "(We expect) no change in rates in this meeting. The inflation target is very ambitious, and I do not see a room for a rate cut," said analyst Anne Francois Blueher of Conseq Finance. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is due to discuss its quarterly inflation report, macroeconomic outlook and monthly monetary policy report at its meeting on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The CNB left its key interest rates unchanged at its last policy meeting on March 30, but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the crown at around 35.65 to the euro, knocking the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more than two percent lower. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member Miroslav Hnrcir said on Tuesday that the bank's end-2001 net inflation target implied the bank would keep a roughly neutral monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  The CNB has an end-2000 net inflation target of 3.5-5.5 percent, but it and independent analysts widely expect this year's result to end at the bottom of, or below, this range. \par \par \uc2  The CNB has a long-term, end-2005 target of 1.0-3.0 percent as part of plans to prepare the \b \highlight22\uc2 Czech Republic\b0 \highlight\uc2  for European Union membership. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  SEEN UNLIKELY \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers were more worried about possible CNB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  than an interest rate cut. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said that a move against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely despite the crown's firming in recent days to around 36.2 to the euro, its strongest level since the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There are no signals that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is thinking of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The element of a surprise is gone, and the bank would not be able to duplicate the success of March 30," said ING Barings analyst Boris Gomez. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reached a record low against the dollar on Wednesday and was trading at 39.38/42 at 1145 GMT, with dealers attributing its dip against the greenback to easing on the euro/dollar. The crown was bid at 36.23 to the euro. \par \par \uc2  "(The CNB) may rather make a statement about the (exchange) rate...The rate of the crown/dollar is weak. It would not be appropriate if they also tried to push the crown lower versus the euro," said dealer Marek Ratkovsky of Ceska Sportielna. ((Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2419-0477, fax 420-2-2422-9935, prague.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw4q01dpy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
