\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - CZECH REPUBLIC, AUSTRIA - NOV 27. \b0\par\par\uc2 812 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HOSPODARSKE NOVINY - For the first time since the May \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis, the crown came close to 19.50 crowns to the mark yesterday and closed at 19.46. Experts say the crown could reach 22 to the mark by the end of the year. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expressed disappointment, but did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Czech Republic\b0 \highlight\uc2  yesterday officially established its NATO mission in Brussels. \par \par \uc2  - The federation of agricultural cooperatives and companies expects the agrarian sector to finish this year with a 2.8-billion-crown loss. \par \par \uc2  - The cabinet approved a proclamation to create methods for secrecy with NATO information. \par \par \uc2  - By the end of the year, all Moravia Steel shareholders will leave the management of Trinecke Zelezarny and other subsidiary companies to be replaced by managing teams. \par \par \uc2  - For the first three quarters of this year, Prague Breweries increased exports to Britain by 42 percent and to Germany by 23 percent. MLADA FRONTA DNES - Swedish ambassador Petr Kolar and businessman Michal Kuzimiak, who worked on the election campaign for ODS last year, insist that several politicians in this party new from the beginning that the contraversial donation of 7.5 million crowns was from businessman and former tennis player Milan Srejber. \par \par \uc2  - According to a study among exporters and importers from the Czech Statistical Bureau (CSU), the foreign trade deficit will not exceed 137 billion crowns this year. \par \par \uc2  - A regional commercial court yesterday blocked all bank accounts of Poldi Steel, which currently contain 5.5 million crowns, while 3.5 million of this is a credit from Aero Vodochody. \par \par \uc2  - The cabinet yesterday discussed the proposal of Skoda Auto, which wants to decrease its basic capital by 0.5 billion marks. Industry and Trade Minister Karel Kuhnl said meetings will be held with the management of Volkswagen to discuss this plan. \par \par \uc2  - Yesterday, the cabinet approved a proposal for a new transformation law, according to which cooperatives will settle their debts for deposited property either with securities. \par \par \uc2  - Investicni a Postovni Banka, in the name of the majority shareholder of Radegast brewery, IMP Finance, which owns about 57 percent of Radegast, offered to buy securities from minority shareholders for 4,603 crowns each. \par \par \uc2  - According to a proposal for a new law approved by the cabinet yesterday, insurance for deposits should also apply to corporate accounts from April next year, if the law is approved by parliament. \par \par \uc2  - The cabinet yesterday approved a new business law that should make conditions for entrepreneurs more consise next year and should increase government regulation. PRAVO - From January 1, central heating prices will increase by up to 40 percent, according to material approved by the cabinet yesterday. \par \par \uc2  - Deputy Finance Minister Miroslav Havel said his ministry still considers 10 billion crowns a realistic estimate for this year's budget deficit. \par \par \uc2  - Coalition parties will propose next week that parliament organise a commission to propose changes in regulations for financing political parties. \par \par \uc2  - Wednesday general meetings of two subsidiaries of CKD Praha Holding -- Lokomotivka and Obchodni Sluzby, decided to liquadate these companies on January 1 due to their high losses. LIDOVE NOVINY - Konsolidacni Banka Praha, together with ING Baring Capital Markets, began issuing a third wave of crown bonds on the domestic capital market for five billion crowns. \par \par \uc2  - Coalition parties will collectively propose in the middle of December to reelect Vaclav Havel as president of the Czech Republic. \par \par \uc2  - Communist parliamentary deputees are planning to meet with representatives of their partner parties in Spain, Italy, France and Greece to get these representatives to reject the Czech Republic's entry into NATO. \par \par \uc2  ((Prague newsroom, +420-2-2423-0003, fax +420-2-2422-9935, prague.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  AUSTRIA: \par \par \uc2  VIENNA, Nov 27 (Reuters) - Following are some of the main stories in Austrian newspapers this morning. \par \par \uc2  DIE PRESSE \par \par \uc2  - Most EU-memberstates have shorter periods of naturalisation of immigrants than Austria. \par \par \uc2  - The far-right Freedom Party's campaign to collect 100,000 signatures to force parliamentary debate on an EMU referendum "is going well", said Peter Westenthaler, the Freedom Party's secretary general. \par \par \uc2  - Extended opening hours are not used, a study by an employees association found. \par \par \uc2  DER STANDARD \par \par \uc2  - Conservative People's Party rejects Chancellor Viktor Klima's suggestion of imposing a stricter firearms law. \par \par \uc2  - Revenues in Austria's tourism sector fell 1.9 percent to 84.3 billion schillings from Mai to October compared to the same period last year. \par \par \uc2  KURIER \par \par \uc2  - Trade unions threaten a shopping mall to take it to the constitutional court for its opening hours on Sundays. \par \par \uc2  - Germany's grid company Bayernwerk and Austria's oils and chemicals group OMV offered 4.4 billion schillings for Estag, Stryria's electricity supplier which is due to be privatised. \par \par \uc2  - Formula 1 Grand Prix race in the province Styria was with revenues of 723 million schillings ablsolutely profitable, according to a study by the Austrian Society for Marketing OGM. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limit